      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The full sphere comparison reconstructs integral motivic homotopy groups from all prime completions, combining Ext-completion splitting for abelian groups with finite Adams/Adams-Novikov limits, separate exceptional stem handling and identification of the divisible kernel via the rational unit map and integral motivic-cohomology divisibility. The full native algebraic closure/characteristic-zero conventions and s exclusions are retained; this is the global motivic comparison theorem beyond the old five-lemma-mod-divisibles support. Stiefel and module consequences are context without extra counts.",
